MangoDB executes an aggregation pipeline on the collection using the `aggregate` method defined in `src/collection.ts`. This method processes documents through a sequence of stages, each transforming the document stream, and stages are executed in order. The supported stages include `$match`, `$project`, `$sort`, `$limit`, `$skip`, `$count`, and `$unwind`. The `aggregate` method creates a database context for stages like `$lookup`, `$out`, and `$geoNear`, and returns an `AggregationCursor` for iterating through results. The method is defined as follows:

```typescript
aggregate(pipeline: PipelineStage[], _options?: AggregateOptions): AggregationCursor<T> {
  // Create database context for $lookup, $out, and $geoNear stages
  const dbContext: AggregationDbContext = {
    getCollection: (name: string) => {
      return new MangoCollection(this.dataDir, this.dbName, name);
    },
    getGeoIndexes: async () => {
      return this.indexManager.getGeoIndexes();
    },
  };

  return new AggregationCursor<T>(() => this.readDocuments(), pipeline, dbContext);
}
```
